menu "ASIX USB Ethernet host driver"

    config ASIX_RX_BUFFER_SIZE
        int "RX transfer buffer size (bytes)"
        default 2048
        range 2048 16384
        help
            Size of each bulk IN transfer buffer. The chip is told the
            matching maximum burst (RX_CTL MFB) so it never sends more
            than one buffer holds: 2048, 4096, 8192 or 16384. Values
            between those round down to the next one. Larger buffers let
            the chip pack several frames per transfer, which helps
            throughput at the cost of RAM.

    config ASIX_RX_TRANSFER_COUNT
        int "RX transfers kept in flight"
        default 2
        range 1 8
        help
            Number of bulk IN transfers submitted at once. Two keeps one
            in flight while the other is being unpacked; more smooths
            bursts at the cost of one RX buffer each.

endmenu
